# Shatter

## Overview

{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
Shatter is a top-down space-rock shooter for the browser, played on one wrapping
field of deep space. You pilot a small ship under pure momentum, turning and
thrusting while jagged rocks drift and tumble around you. The larger rocks are
armored and hold together under several hits before they come apart, a Large
into two smaller ones and each of those into smaller ones still, until the last
fragments wink out. Against the ones that will not break in time the ship
carries a single guided torpedo on a slow recharge, which destroys any rock
outright. Clear the field and a denser, faster wave arrives, and an enemy saucer
wanders in to hunt you on a cadence of its own.
{{else}}
Shatter is a top-down space-rock shooter for the browser, played on one wrapping
field of deep space. You pilot a small ship under pure momentum, turning and
thrusting while jagged rocks drift and tumble around you. Firing splits a Large
rock into two smaller ones, and each of those into smaller ones still, until the
last fragments wink out. Clear the field and a denser, faster wave arrives, and
an enemy saucer wanders in to hunt you on a cadence of its own.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
Shatter's defining idea is the gravity well. A star fixed at the centre of the
field pulls on everything that flies ballistically, which is every bullet, every
saucer bullet and every rock. The ship, the saucer, and the torpedo are powered
craft the pull never touches, so the star never wrests the ship out of the
player's hands. Instead it shapes the board: shots bend as they cross the
centre, so a bullet can be curved around the star to strike a rock on its far
side, and rocks travel on curved, wrapping paths that keep the whole field
churning.
{{else}}
Shatter's defining idea is the gravity well. A star fixed at the centre of the
field pulls on everything that flies ballistically, which is every bullet, every
saucer bullet and every rock. The ship and the saucer are powered craft the pull
never touches, so the star never wrests the ship out of the player's hands.
Instead it shapes the board: shots bend as they cross the centre, so a bullet
can be curved around the star to strike a rock on its far side, and rocks travel
on curved, wrapping paths that keep the whole field churning.
{{/if}}

The core of the star is solid. The ship slides along it rather than through it, a
shot that reaches it is absorbed, and a rock the star swallows re-appears from the
edge of the field, so the well stirs the board without ever emptying it.

Shatter has its own name, look, and rules, and its art, branding, and design are
original to it.

